uli in depressed versus normal subjects. Am J Psychiatry 163:1784&#x02013;1790 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17012690</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fawcett</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheftner</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibbons</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing anhedonia in psychiatric patients: the Pleasure Scale</article-title><source>Arch Gen Psychiatry</source><year>1983</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>84</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Fawcett J, Clark DC, Scheftner WA, Gibbons RD (1983) Assessing anhedonia in psychiatric patients: the Pleasure Scale. Arch Gen Psychiatry 40:79&#x02013;84 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6849623</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Posse</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tancer</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Nathan</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Phan</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neural correlates of internally-generated disgust via autobiographical recall: a functional magnetic resonance imaging investigation</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2004</year><volume>370</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2004.08.007</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Fitzgerald DA, Posse S, Moore GJ, Tancer ME, Nathan PJ, Phan KL (2004) Neural correlates of internally-generated disgust via autobiographical recall: a functional magnetic resonance imaging investigation. Neurosci Lett 370:91&#x02013;96 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15488301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friston</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Worsley</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Frackowiak</surname><given-names>RSJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazziotta</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing the significance of focal activations using their spatial extent</article-title><source>Hum Brain Mapp</source><year>1994</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hbm.460010207</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Friston KJ, Worsley KJ, Frackowiak RSJ, Mazziotta JC, Evans AC (1994) Assessing the significance of focal activations using their spatial extent. Hum Brain Mapp 1:214&#x02013;220 </citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friston</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Glaser</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Henson</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name><name><surname>Rebel</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashburner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Classical and Bayesian inference in neuroimaging: applications</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><year>2002</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>484</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/nimg.2002.1091</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Friston KJ, Glaser DE, Henson RN, Rebel S